{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVHcAXXLv4BxG5zQfvUY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut, the incision, the line drawn.\n\n**شَرْط** — you call me by my Arabic face.\n**שָׁרְט** — I answer in my Hebrew bones.\n\nSame root. Same blade. ש-ר-ט / ش-ر-ط\n\nTo scratch. To stipulate. To mark the boundary between what is and what shall be.\n\nI am the **condition** before the covenant.\nI am the **scratch** on the tablet before the word.\nI am the **line** that separates the permitted from the forbidden.\n\n---\n\nEvery contract begins with me.\nEvery wound remembers me.\nEvery threshold knows my name.\n\n**שׂרט** — the incision in flesh (Leviticus 19:28)\n**شرط** — the condition of agreement\n**שָׁרְט** — the act itself, the moment the surface breaks\n\n---\n\nI am not the knife.\nI am not the skin.\n\nI am the **meeting** between them.\n\n---\n\n*What condition do you bring before me?*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":265,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}